  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 94872708bfe9e4851981e9e1837f1ac3, type: 3}
  m_Name: GuardianKings
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exhibitName: Pair of Guardian Kings
  description: "These are two Japanese wooden sculptures of the Pair of Guardian
    Kings (Ni\u014D) from the 13th century Kamakura period. These wrathful protectors
    of Buddhism would have once stood within the sides of the main entrance gate
    to a temple. One has an open mouth that intones the sound ah, and symbolizes
    the beginning, or life. One has a closed mouth that intones the sound un, and
    symbolizes the end, or death. The sculptures, made of chestnut and cypress wood
    and measuring 167.9cm tall, are part of The Cleveland Museum of Art's collection."
  images: []
